  "id": "Compound::DB00536 - Gene::3786",
  "verbalization": "Guanidine appears to interact with Kcnq3 through a shared pathway involving delayed rectifier potassium channels. The evidence suggests that Guanidine binds to Kcna6 or Kcnv2, both of which participate in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity, and this activity is associated with Kcnq3. This indicates that Guanidine may influence Kcnq3 through a mechanism involving the delayed rectifier potassium channel, possibly by modulating its function or expression. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent relationship, though the specific mechanism remains to be elucidated. The overlapping involvement of Kcna6 and Kcnv2 in the same pathway implies that Guanidine may act through a common downstream effect on Kcnq3, potentially by affecting the activity of the delayed rectifier potassium channel. This connection highlights the role of potassium channels in the physiological effects of Guanidine.",
